      "original": "$z_1-7=3p$",
      "corrected": "$z_1+7=3p$",
      "reason": "The frozen A=(1,2,-7), B=(x_1,y_1,z_1), and AB=OB-OA force AB=(x_1-1,y_1-2,z_1+7). Thus AB=p(12,4,3) forces z_1+7=3p. The printed subtraction contradicts the same preceding identity. Independent derivation gives p=5/169, B=(229/169,358/169,-1168/169), plane residual zero and distance5/13. Only this component sign is corrected; source body and figure11 remain unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "p0162-ex28-foot-point",
