        "pdf_sha256": "1900be5207d00404f64e5a40ab855fbfb8495bd2a06c5ce295ae0e145444578a"
      },
      "original": "$p(x_1,y_1,z_1)$",
      "corrected": "$B(x_1,y_1,z_1)$",
      "reason": "The same solution defines (x_1,y_1,z_1) as the coordinates of the perpendicular foot B; p is the scalar in AB=p n, not a named point. Plane membership therefore refers to B(x_1,y_1,z_1). The independently derived B lies on the plane with p=5/169 and distance5/13. Only the point referent is corrected; source body and figure11 remain unchanged."
    }
